From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:26:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/45] Send the 3D view state in the Specula feed

Feed format v6. Each turn entity grows from 28 to 64 bytes: its height,
and what its VisualActor shows (actor, seed, variant set, animation with
its once flag, speed and sync repeat/offset), and its construction
progress. Actor and animation names and variant keys and selections go
out once as string records; whole variant sets go out once as variant set
records, so entities refer to both by index.

The construction previews of foundations, local "construction|" entities,
are now sent too: they are the rising building the game draws.

ICmpVisual and ICmpPosition gain C++-only getters for state their
components already keep. They are not exposed to scripts, so the
simulation and its hash are unchanged.
